From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] replay: log where a diverged checkpoint differs

"Diverged by frame N from byte M" names one byte. Which fields differ,
and how many, is what tells a host pointer in the state (two bytes at
an 8-byte stride) from an emulation divergence (RAM all over) from a
timing leak (a sound chip's counters). Log the first eight differing
ranges with both sides' bytes, and the total.

Signed-off-by: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
---
--- a/input/bsv/bsvmovie.c
+++ b/input/bsv/bsvmovie.c
@@ -838,8 +838,27 @@
          while (i < size && state[i] == handle->cur_save[i])
             i++;
          if (i < size)
+         {
+            size_t j = i, n = 0, total = 0;
             RARCH_WARN("[Replay] Diverged by frame %lld: the state differs from the checkpoint from byte %zu of %zu.\n",
                   (long long)handle->frame_counter, i, size);
+            while (j < size)
+            {
+               if (state[j] != handle->cur_save[j])
+               {
+                  size_t k = j;
+                  while (k < size && state[k] != handle->cur_save[k]) k++;
+                  total += k - j;
+                  if (n < 8)
+                     RARCH_WARN("[Replay]   [%zu,%zu) state %02x%02x%02x%02x checkpoint %02x%02x%02x%02x\n",
+                           j, k, state[j], state[j+1], state[j+2], state[j+3],
+                           handle->cur_save[j], handle->cur_save[j+1], handle->cur_save[j+2], handle->cur_save[j+3]);
+                  n++; j = k;
+               }
+               else j++;
+            }
+            RARCH_WARN("[Replay]   %zu differing bytes in %zu ranges\n", total, n);
+         }
          else
             RARCH_LOG("[Replay] Checkpoint at frame %lld matches.\n",
                   (long long)handle->frame_counter);
